{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"850779735780491276","content":"Main NPC: Gaillardia, a Dryad \nGaillardia is the mother of Herb, of Herb’s Herbs. They live together in this cozy little hut on a seaside cliff. Gaillardia is agoraphobic and never leaves her home and the surrounding gardens. She is no nonsense, a little grumbly, and is devoted to protecting her grove.\nOn the Edge of Illo’fae stands a cozy looking cottage nestled atop a seaside cliff. It is surrounded by all manner of trees, flowers, and other plants. Butterflies flit from bud to bud, catching the ocean breeze. \nInside the cottage is cluttered with drying plants of all kinds, bubbling pots, and shelves and shelves of magical components. You see a cauldron bearing relief scenes of various heroes embossed on its sides. \nGaillardia can bring one person back to life with this cauldron of rebirth every 7 days. This requires 200lbs (10g) of salt, various items of importance to the character being brought back, and one fae deal of the DMs choosing. \nOnce adventurers are out gathering the necessary components Gaillardia will cast speak with dead on the PC being brought back. If a deal is not struck by the end of her questions, she will not bring them back. \nIf a deal is struck, and ingredients successfully gathered, the spell will be complete 8 hours after the last ingredient is placed. Characters are encouraged to speak on behalf of their friend, reminding of who they are, what is left to accomplish, etc while the process is underway.","created_at":"2021-06-11T01:23:16.912000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"852719606324789278","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
